HEAD is now at 2005b45 devnet: regenerate the address book for the 2026-09-17 fresh genesis The genesis reset wiped every script-deployed contract, so deploy-testnet-infra.sh redeployed the whole app stack and wrote the new addresses back: 23 eXYZ stablecoins, StablecoinImpl, StablecoinManager(+Impl), GitAttestationRegistry, Uniswap V2 (factory, router, 45 pools), V3 (factory + periphery) and V4 (Permit2, PoolManager, periphery). ConsensusRegistry, Issuance and StakeManager are genesis-assigned and unchanged. Two entries are deliberate rather than mechanical:   .WTEL is now the genesis vanity address 0x00000000000000000000000000000000000037E1.   It previously held the pre-genesis CREATE2 value, which on a freshly genesised chain   has no code -- so has_code() would have failed, step 4 would have deployed a SECOND   WTEL there, and every Uniswap router would have been wired to the duplicate instead of   the one the chain actually mints into. script/README.md:109 called for this at the next   reset; this is that reset. Step 4 now correctly reports "WTEL already deployed, skipping".   .admin was already pointed at the deploying EOA in the previous commit. Verified post-deploy: every key tn-transaction-generator treats as mandatory (src/deployments.rs) returns non-empty eth_getCode, and 22 of the 45 V2 pools hold reserves after SeedTestnetLPs. The two wTEL pools are empty -- the admin holds native TEL, not wrapped -- so TEL-denominated swap paths have no liquidity yet.
